---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Scientific Library"
  description="The PeptiBloom Scientific Library is a public research resource built to make evidence, uncertainty, provenance and unanswered questions inspectable."
>
  <section class="page-hero section">
    <div class="site-frame page-hero__grid page-hero__grid--library">
      <div class="page-hero__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Scientific Library</p>
        <h1>Research should be easier to inspect than marketing.</h1>
        <p class="page-hero__lead">PeptiBloom scientific entries make evidence, uncertainty and provenance visible. Compound pages appear only after completing the approved scientific and editorial review path.</p>
        <div class="hero__actions" aria-label="Library actions">
          <a class="button button--primary" href="#published-entries">Explore the library</a>
          <a class="editorial-link" href="/methodology/">Read the methodology <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <aside class="library-cover" aria-labelledby="library-cover-title">
        <div class="library-cover__topline"><span>PeptiBloom Scientific Library</span><span aria-hidden="true">01</span></div>
        <div class="library-cover__halo" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <p class="surface-kicker">Reading standard</p>
        <h2 id="library-cover-title">What is known. What is not. Where it comes from.</h2>
        <div class="library-cover__footer"><span>Evidence</span><span>Uncertainty</span><span>Provenance</span></div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--quiet" id="published-entries" aria-labelledby="entries-title">
    <div class="site-frame">
      <div class="section-heading reading-column"><p class="eyebrow">Reviewed entries</p><h2 id="entries-title">The library begins with evidence, not catalogue size.</h2><p>Each entry is revision-controlled and reviewed before it is surfaced here.</p></div>
      <a class="entry-card" href="/library/retatrutide/">
        <div><p class="surface-kicker">Investigational · Evidence cutoff 03 Sep 2026</p><h3>Retatrutide</h3><p>Triple GIPR / GLP-1R / GCGR agonist with peer-reviewed human phase 1b, phase 2 and phase 3 evidence.</p></div>
        <div class="entry-card__meta"><span>Human efficacy <strong>Solid within scope</strong></span><span>Long-term outcomes <strong>Unresolved</strong></span><span>Preparation evidence <strong>Insufficient</strong></span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b></div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-labelledby="library-principles-title">
    <div class="site-frame"><div class="section-heading reading-column"><p class="eyebrow">Library principles</p><h2 id="library-principles-title">What every PeptiBloom scientific entry makes visible.</h2></div>
      <div class="library-principles library-principles--cards">
        <article class="library-principle"><span><small>01</small>Evidence</span><p>What the available research can support — without extending beyond it.</p></article>
        <article class="library-principle"><span><small>02</small>Uncertainty</span><p>What remains theoretical, disputed, incomplete or unknown.</p></article>
        <article class="library-principle"><span><small>03</small>Provenance</span><p>Where information comes from and how a reader can trace it back.</p></article>
        <article class="library-principle"><span><small>04</small>Contradictions</span><p>Where sources or findings do not align cleanly.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft" aria-labelledby="next-title">
    <div class="site-frame method-callout"><div class="method-callout__marker" aria-hidden="true"><span>01</span><span>04</span></div><div class="reading-column"><p class="eyebrow">How to read PeptiBloom</p><h2 id="next-title">Start with the method, then follow the sources.</h2><p>The methodology explains how PeptiBloom approaches provenance, interpretation, contradictions and the boundary between scientific information and commercial information.</p><a class="button button--primary" href="/methodology/">Read the methodology</a></div></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
.entry-card{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.25fr) minmax(18rem,.75fr);gap:clamp(2rem,6vw,5rem);padding:clamp(1.5rem,4vw,3rem);border:1px solid var(--color-hairline);border-radius:var(--radius-large);background:var(--color-paper);box-shadow:var(--shadow-paper);color:var(--color-ink);text-decoration:none}.entry-card:hover{border-color:rgba(122,63,104,.35);color:var(--color-ink)}.entry-card h3{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.2rem)}.entry-card p:not(.surface-kicker){color:var(--color-muted-ink)}.entry-card__meta{display:grid;gap:.8rem;align-content:center;font-family:var(--font-system);font-size:.86rem}.entry-card__meta span{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;padding-bottom:.7rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-hairline)}.entry-card__meta strong{color:var(--color-mulberry);text-align:right}.entry-card__meta b{justify-self:end;font-size:1.8rem;color:var(--color-mulberry)}@media(max-width:760px){.entry-card{grid-template-columns:1fr}.entry-card__meta span{display:grid}.entry-card__meta strong{text-align:left}}
</style>